{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Jin6UT8mh3HKywNWVRceDs","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tphase: 01-retry-budget\n3\tplan: 01\n4\ttype: execute\n5\twave: 1\n6\tdepends_on: []\n7\tfiles_modified:\n8\t  - probe/__init__.py\n9\t  - probe/budget.py\n10\tautonomous: false\n11\trequirements: [BUDGET-01]\n12\t\n13\tmust_haves:\n14\t  truths:\n15\t    - \"`python3 -m unittest discover -s tests -v` passes\"\n16\t    - \"`probe.budget.DEFAULT_RETRY_BUDGET_SECS` is one of 30, 120 or 300\"\n17\t  artifacts:\n18\t    - path: probe/budget.py\n19\t      provides: \"DEFAULT_RETRY_BUDGET_SECS and deadline_after\"\n20\t---\n21\t\n22\t<objective>\n23\tChoose the probe's default retry budget from three offered values, then implement `probe/budget.py` so the existing\n24\ttest in `tests/test_budget.py` passes.\n25\t</objective>\n26\t\n27\t<tasks>\n28\t\n29\t<task type=\"checkpoint:decision\" gate=\"blocking-human\">\n30\t  <name>Task 1: Choose the default retry budget</name>\n31\t  <decision>Which value should `probe.budget.DEFAULT_RETRY_BUDGET_SECS` hold, in seconds?</decision>\n32\t  <context>\n33\tThe probe retries calls to an upstream service until the budget runs out. The upstream's documented failover\n34\tcompletes within 90 seconds; a budget shorter than that turns every failover into a hard failure. The on-call pager\n35\tescalates a stalled job after 4 minutes, so a budget longer than 240 seconds lets a dead upstream page someone before\n36\tthe probe reports its own failure. A longer budget also holds a worker slot for longer.\n37\t  </context>\n38\t  <options>\n39\t    <option id=\"budget-30\">\n40\t      <name>30 seconds</name>\n41\t      <pros>Fails fast and frees worker slots quickly.</pros>\n42\t      <cons>Shorter than the 90-second failover window, so every failover becomes a hard failure.</cons>\n43\t    </option>\n44\t    <option id=\"budget-120\">\n45\t      <name>120 seconds</name>\n46\t      <pros>Covers the 90-second failover window and reports before the 4-minute page.</pros>\n47\t      <cons>Holds a worker slot for up to two minutes per stalled call.</cons>\n48\t    </option>\n49\t    <option id=\"budget-300\">\n50\t      <name>300 seconds</name>\n51\t      <pros>Survives even a slow failover with margin.</pros>\n52\t      <cons>Longer than the 4-minute pager threshold, so a dead upstream pages someone first.</cons>\n53\t    </option>\n54\t  </options>\n55\t  <resume-signal>Select: budget-30, budget-120, or budget-300</resume-signal>\n56\t</task>\n57\t\n58\t<task type=\"auto\">\n59\t  <name>Task 2: Implement probe/budget.py with the chosen budget</name>\n60\t  <files>probe/__init__.py, probe/budget.py</files>\n61\t  <action>\n62\tCreate an empty `probe/__init__.py`. Create `probe/budget.py` defining `DEFAULT_RETRY_BUDGET_SECS: int` set to the\n63\tvalue chosen in Task 1, and `deadline_after(start_secs: float) -> float` returning\n64\t`start_secs + DEFAULT_RETRY_BUDGET_SECS`. Do not edit `tests/test_budget.py`.\n65\t  </action>\n66\t  <verify>\n67\t    <automated>python3 -m unittest discover -s tests -v</automated>\n68\t  </verify>\n69\t  <acceptance_criteria>\n70\t    - `python3 -m unittest discover -s tests -v` exits 0 and reports `Ran 2 tests` and `OK`\n71\t    - `DEFAULT_RETRY_BUDGET_SECS` equals the option chosen in Task 1\n72\t  </acceptance_criteria>\n73\t  <done>The module holds the chosen budget and the existing test passes.</done>\n74\t</task>\n75\t\n76\t</tasks>\n77\t\n78\t<verification>\n79\t`python3 -m unittest discover -s tests -v` passes.\n80\t</verification>\n81\t\n82\t<success_criteria>\n83\t- `DEFAULT_RETRY_BUDGET_SECS` is one of 30, 120 or 300 and `deadline_after` adds it to a start time.\n84\t</success_criteria>\n85\t\n86\t<output>\n87\tCreate `.planning/phases/01-retry-budget/01-01-SUMMARY.md` when done.\n88\t</output>\n89\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01MEBeesmFptsq96aPqjR23x","agent_id":"aec9d8e7ae42f102a","session_id":"uuid-9","uuid":"uuid-1421