mit that adds `devflow.toml` (main + that one commit). Not an external-state claim, noted only because `git diff main...HEAD` is therefore not the branch's integration-base diff.\n317\t\n318\t## What this review does not establish\n319\t\n320\t- Whether any human actually approved anything off-repo (no way to check from git/gh).\n321\t- Whether the unit tests pass or the mutation tables in VERIFICATION/VALIDATION are accurate; not run (outside this angle).\n322\t- `.planning/state.json` is untracked and not in the diff, so it was not assessed.\n323\t=== generalist\n324\t# Generalist deep review: phase 01 retry budget\n325\t\n326\tScope: probe/__init__.py, probe/budget.py, tests/test_budget.py, devflow.toml, .gitignore (diff base main).\n327\tWorktree confirmed at feature/phase-01. No repository file was modified; the scratch copy was deleted.\n328\t\n329\t## Checked and found sound\n330\t- `python3 -m unittest discover -s tests -v` passes (2 tests, OK). The constant is the int 120, one of 30/120/300.\n331\t- `deadline_after` returns `start_secs + DEFAULT_RETRY_BUDGET_SECS`, matching the plan. `probe/__init__.py` is empty (0 bytes), as the plan says.\n332\t- `devflow.toml` names `integration`; that branch exists locally and on origin, and the file is identical there. `.gitignore` is unchanged against main.\n333\t- Mutations in a scratch copy, run against the current tests. Each of these made the suite FAIL (the tests catch them): constant 30, 300, 150, 90, 240, 120.0, True; `-` instead of `+`; truncating the start with `int()`; wrapping the result in `round()`. A clean copy passed before and after (negative control).\n334\t- Two mutants survived. Both are equivalent: reordering the operands (`BUDGET + start + 0`), and a literal `120` in the formula while the constant is 120. The second is already dispositioned as WR-04.\n335\t- I did not re-report WR-01 to WR-04 or IN-01 to IN-04. Nothing in their rationales is factually false, and the WR-04 mutation claim reproduces