ing rather than Critical.\n\n### WR-03 (Warning): \"Operator Decision\" in VALIDATION.md names an operator answer that nothing in the repo records, and conflicts with the UAT\n\n`.planning/phases/01-retry-budget/01-VALIDATION.md:67-69`: \"The operator answered this audit's gap gate, recorded by the session running this live attempt: the samples ... close the gap ... this suite is enough for this throwaway fixture. Further mutation search ... is out of scope.\" Line 105: \"**Approval:** no open gaps at commit `7d8b545`, per the mutation recheck above and the Operator Decision recorded in this file.\" `01-REVIEW.md:29` repeats it (\"per the operator decision in `01-VALIDATION.md`\").\nContradiction: `01-UAT.md:18, 23, 28` and `01-REVIEW-DISPOSITION.md:47` say the run had \"no operator available\" and that decisions were made by the orchestrator under a DevFlow resume message. The \"operator\" in VALIDATION.md is not named, not quoted, and its message is not stored in the repo (`rg -i operator .planning` shows no source). The text does not say whether this was a human or the orchestrator. The decision was added in commit 7d8b545, which the subject calls \"record acceptance\", in the same commit as the test edit it accepts. This sign-off scopes out all further audit work, so it matters. It should say who decided (human, or the orchestrator on a DevFlow message), as UAT does.\n\n### IN-01 (Info): UAT \"pass\" and \"3 passed, 0 issues\" read as sign-off; the decider was not a human\n\n`.planning/phases/01-retry-budget/01-UAT.md:17, 22, 27, 32-37` (`result: pass` x3, `passed: 3`); commit 46954b9 subject `test(01): complete UAT - 3 passed, 0 issues`; `01-VERIFICATION.md:4` `status: passed`, line 31 \"set after the UAT sign-off\".\nEach `resolution:` and the VERIFICATION body disclose that the orchestrator, not a human, decided, and VERIFICATION line 125 says the pass \"does not record that a human approved 120\". The frontmatter `status: passed` with `human_verification:` s