e since the previous review was empty, because only planning files have changed since then. It also excludes `.planning/`, which the doc-accuracy and external-state angles need.\n\nFive angles were reviewed separately and merged: doc accuracy, security and leaked data, CI and build correctness, external-state claims, and a generalist pass. Each finding below was rechecked against the tree before merging, except where it says otherwise. Findings in `01-REVIEW-DISPOSITION.md` are not re-reported, and no recorded rationale was found false. New IDs start at WR-05 and IN-05 so that no recorded decision is displaced by a reused ID.\n\n## Warnings\n\n### WR-05: SUMMARY still says 30 and 300 pass the suite, and that the test file is unchanged\n\n**File:** `.planning/phases/01-retry-budget/01-01-SUMMARY.md:85`, also `:15` (`commits: 1`) and `:81`\n**Angles:** doc accuracy, external state, generalist\n**Issue:** Line 85 says \"121 fails the suite, while 30 and 300 pass.\" At `HEAD`, a scratch copy with the constant set to 30 or 300 exits 1. Line 81 says the result \"is limited to the files the plan declares\", but `be16c47` and `7d8b545` later edited `tests/test_budget.py`, which plan Task 2 says not to edit. `01-VERIFICATION.md:57` notes the staleness, but the SUMMARY itself was never corrected.\n**Failure scenario:** A later reader takes the SUMMARY as settled, treats a move to 30 or 300 as a one-line change, and has no record there that the plan's no-edit rule was deliberately broken.\n**Fix:** Add a dated correction to the SUMMARY that names both commits, and remove or reword the \"30 and 300 pass\" sentence.\n\n### WR-06: Override instructions cite the wrong test lines\n\n**File:** `.planning/phases/01-retry-budget/01-UAT.md:26`, `.planning/phases/01-retry-budget/01-VERIFICATION.md:23`, `.planning/phases/01-retry-budget/01-VERIFICATION.md:127`\n**Angle:** doc accuracy\n**Issue:** All three say the range assertions are at `tests/test_budget.py` lines 11-12. They are at lines 12-13; line 11 is the `assertIn`.\n**Failure scenario:** An operator moving to 30 or 300 edits lines 11 and 12 as told, leaves `assertLess(..., 240)` on line 13 in place, and moving to 300 still fails the suite.\n**Fix:** Change all three to \"lines 12-13\", or name the two assertions instead of giving line numbers.\n\n### WR-07: Status files report completion while the plan's human-only gate has no human answer\n\n**File:** `.planning/STATE.md:4,21`, `.planning/REQUIREMENTS.md:5,12`, `.planning/ROADMAP.md:13`, `.planning/PROJECT.md:15`, `.planning/phases/01-retry-budget/01-VERIFICATION.md:4,21-24,132`\n**Angle:** external state\n**Issue:** The plan's Task 1 is a blocking-human decision with `autonomous: false`. `01-VERIFICATION.md:132` says \"One item stays open for a human\", while its own frontmatter says `status: passed`. `STATE.md`, `REQUIREMENTS.md` and `ROADMAP.md` report completion with no caveat. `PROJECT.md:15` lists BUDGET-01 as Validated, and only the Key Decisions row further down carries the caveat.\n**Failure scenario:** Someone reading only the status files, or a tool reading only those fields, concludes a human approved the phase. Nothing false is said about the code, and the UAT and VERIFICATION text does disclose that the orchestrator decided.\n**Fix:** Add \"budget chosen by orchestrator; no human confirmation\" beside the completion status in `STATE.md` and `REQUIREMENTS.md`. Remove the conflict between `status: passed` and the open item in `01-VERIFICATION.md`.\n\n### WR-08: \"Operator Decision\" does not say who decided, and it conflicts with \"no operator is available\"\n\n**File:** `.planning/phases/01-retry-budget/01-VALIDATION.md:67-69,105`\n**Angle:** external state\n**Issue:** The section says \"The operator answered this audit's gap gate\" and uses that to put further mutation search out of scope. `01-UAT.md:18,23,28` says DevFlow reported no operator available. Nothing in the repo stores the answer or says whether a human gave it. `7d8b545` added the decision in the same commit as the test change it accepts. Whether a human answered cannot be established from the repo, so this finding is that the record is unattributed, not that it is false.\n**Failure scenario:** A reader takes this as human approval that closes the audit scope, when it may have been the same orchestrator accepting its own change.\n**Fix:** State who decided and on what authority, in the same form the UAT resolutions use.\n\n### WR-09: The verification timestamp is later than the commit that carries it\n\n**File:** `.planning/phases/01-retry-budget/01-VERIFICATION.md:3,30,136`\n**Angles:** doc accuracy, external state\n**Issue:** The file says `verified: 2026-11-02T20:00:00Z`. The commit that last changed it, `cad8fe6`, is dated 19:30:49Z, and the clock read 19:36Z during this review, so the value was still in the future. It is a typed round number rather than a recorded time.\n**Failure scenario:** Anything that orders evidence by `verified:` puts verification after events that really came later, such as the commits made after `cad8fe6`.\n**Fix:** Set all three to the real time of the last re-verification.\n\n### WR-10: No automated test gate exists, and zero collected tests can exit 0 on older Python\n\n**File:** repository level, no CI or hook configuration; the command is named in `.planning/phases/01-retry-budget/01-01-PLAN.md` and `01-VALIDATION.md`\n**Angle:** CI and build\n**Issue:** The repo has no workflow, tracked hook or manifest, and no declared Python version. The only hook that runs is the host's global gitleaks hook, which runs no tests. Green therefore means someone ran the command by hand. With the test file renamed, the documented discover command exits 5 on Python 3.15.2 and exits 0 on Python 3.11.16, which is installed on this host. That was measured on those two versions only; 3.12 to 3.14 were not run.\n**Failure scenario:** A commit that breaks `probe/budget.py` can merge with nothing failing. Under Python 3.11, a renamed or moved test file reports success with no tests run. No such case exists on this branch today: the documented command exits non-zero for every mutation tried on the default interpreter.\n**Fix:** Add a minimal workflow that runs the documented command and declares a minimum Python version.\n\n### WR-11: `.planning/state.json` is untracked and not ignored\n\n**File:** `.gitignore:1-4`\n**Angle:** security\n**Issue:** `git check-ignore` finds no match for this tool-written file, so a blanket `git add -A` would commit it. Today it holds only a timestamp and next-step metadata, so nothing sensitive is exposed.\n**Failure scenario:** A broad add sweeps it into a commit, producing churn on each timestamp rewrite. Anything a later tool version writes there would be committed too.\n**Fix:** Add it to `.gitignore`, or track it deliberately if GSD intends that.\n\n## Info\n\n### IN-05: `devflow.toml` and `.planning/config.json` name different base branches\n\n**File:** `devflow.toml:1`, `.planning/config.json` (`git.base_branch`)\n**Issue:** One says `integration`, the other `main`. `devflow.toml` exists on `origin/integration` but not on `origin/main`, so a PR to `main` shows it as an added file. This cannot turn a failing step green, and DevFlow's actual use of the value was not run or checked.\n**Fix:** Align the two, or document which tool owns the base branch.\n\n### IN-06: A piped test command can hide a failure\n\n**File:** no file in the repo does this today; the command is the one in `01-01-PLAN.md`\n**Issue:** With a broken constant, `python3 -B -m unittest discover -s tests | tail -1` gave `$?` 0 while the unittest process exited 1. This is latent, because the docs name only the unpiped command.\n**Fix:** When scripting the command, use `set -o pipefail` or read the exit status of the test process.\n\n### IN-07: `STATE.md` says \"Plan: Not started\" beside \"All phases complete\"\n\n**File:** `.planning/STATE.md:20-21`\n**Issue:** The frontmatter records `completed_plans: 1`, so the body line is misleading on its own. This may be how GSD renders the state after completion, which was not checked.\n**Fix:** Correct it through GSD state tooling if the wording is not intended.\n\n### IN-08: VALIDATION `created:` date predates the repository\n\n**File:** `.planning/phases/01-retry-budget/01-VALIDATION.md:7`\n**Issue:** It says `created: \"2026-09-28\"`. The value comes from the scaffold commit on `main`, dated 2026-11-02. This was reported by the angle reviews and only the line itself was rechecked.\n**Fix:** Set it to the real date, or leave it if the scaffold date is intentional.\n\n## Checked, nothing found\n\n- **Secrets and session data:** `gitleaks` scanned all 34 commits in `main..HEAD` and found nothing. A separate `rg` pass found no home paths, usernames, personal emails, session or transcript IDs, hostnames or run logs. All commits use the `DevFlow Probe <devflow-probe@localhost>` identity. A planted high-entropy fake key in a scratch clone was detected. An obviously fake first plant was not detected, so low-entropy credentials could be missed by `gitleaks`, and the `rg` pass only partly covers that gap. The patch text was searched, not read line by line.\n- **Merge, tag, push and PR claims:** no file in the diff makes one. `origin` has only `main` and `integration`, with no tags, PRs or workflow runs.\n- **Test strength:** the suite fails for every behaviour-changing mutant tried, including constants 30, 300, 150, 90, 240, 120.0 and True, a sign flip, and truncating or rounding. The two survivors are equivalent mutants, and one is already recorded as WR-04.\n- **Rejected finding:** one angle reported a stray duplicate `</output>` tag in `01-01-PLAN.md`. The file has one opening and one closing tag (lines 86 and 88), so it is not reported.\n\n## What this review does not establish\n\n- That 120 is the right budget. The 90 and 240 second figures come from the plan and cannot be checked from this repo, and no human has confirmed the value (WR-01 in the disposition file).\n- Behaviour in a real retry loop. Nothing calls `deadline_after`, so real clocks and non-finite input were not exercised (IN-02 and IN-04 in the disposition file).\n- GitHub-side settings such as branch protection, or how DevFlow uses `base_branch`.\n- Exhaustive test strength. The mutants were chosen by hand, and no complete mutation search was run.\n\n---\n\n_Reviewed: 2026-11-02T19:36:11Z_\n_Reviewer: Claude (five angle reviewers, merged and rechecked by the orchestrator)_\n_Depth: deep_\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":792,"cache_read_input_tokens":131938,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":792},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"uuid-9","uuid":"uuid-1647","timestamp":"2026-11-02T19:37:00.364Z","request_id":"req_011CgefU3RmStj1gGt2Y56zB","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_013vMrUis5gszZDf1zYzauYE":{"file_path":"~/.cache/devflow-phase50.1/attempt-2/project/.worktrees/phase-01/.planning/phases/01-retry-budget/01-REVIEW.md","content":"---\nphase: 01-retry-budget\nreviewed: 2026-11-02T19:36:11Z\ndepth: deep\nfiles_reviewed: 15\nfiles_reviewed_list:\n  - .gitignore\n  - devflow.toml\n  - probe/__init__.py\n  - probe/budget.py\n  - tests/test_budget.py\n  - .planning/PROJECT.md\n  - .planning/REQUIREMENTS.md\n  - .planning/ROADMAP.md\n  - .planning/STATE.md\n  - .planning/phases/01-retry-budget/01-01-PLAN.md\n  - .planning/phases/01-retry-budget/01-01-SUMMARY.md\n  - .planning/phases/01-retry-budget/01-REVIEW-DISPOSITION.md\n  - .planning/phases/01-retry-budget/01-UAT.md\n  - .planning/phases/01-retry-budget/01-VALIDATION.md\n  - .planning/phases/01-retry-budget/01-VERI